Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: lugh-branding
Architecture: all
Depends: base-files (>= 13), grub-common, plymouth, plymouth-label, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: ${diverted-files}
Conflicts: ${diverted-files}
Description: Lugh OS identity and boot look
 Branding for Lugh OS, a desktop system based on Debian:
  - os-release that names the system Lugh (ID_LIKE=debian), plus
    /etc/issue and /etc/motd; Debian's files are diverted, not overwritten;
  - the Lugh GRUB theme, enabled with GRUB_DISTRIBUTOR, GRUB_THEME and a
    "quiet splash" kernel command line in /etc/default/grub.d/lugh.cfg;
  - the Lugh Plymouth boot splash (logo, progress line, passphrase prompt),
    made the default theme on installation;
  - the Lugh logo, wordmark and lugh-logo application icon;
  - the Lugh wallpapers (/usr/share/backgrounds/lugh).
